WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.850
A young man traveled across the ocean to study music.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:11.560
In a far off country, he met a very small and extraordinary creature.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.640
The tiny creature was injured, so feeling pity for it, he treated it.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.700
Upon doing so...

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.410
I owe you my life.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:28.110
For this, I will grant the blessing of music to the school you build.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.270
Now, some time has passed.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.140
Another extraordinary encounter has taken place.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.240
But... his piano-playing is amazing...

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.080
The Waltz of the Bewildered Heart

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.790
Ow...

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:48.280
That was dangerous. Animals can see me sometimes.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:54.790
Anyway, Kahoko Hino... Are you progressing with your preparations for the competition?

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.910
I'm not quite there yet.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.030
There's going to be four selections, I can't wait!

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:04.970
Maybe <i>you</i> can't wait, Lili...

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.580
Did you say something?

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.240
I said maybe <i>you</i> can't wait, Lili.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:17.140
What the heck? You're freaking me out.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:20.070
That's the first time you called me by my name!

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.040
Is that so?

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.170
It sure is!

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.230
Up till now, you've looked at me like some suspicious creature,

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.070
never calling me by my real name...

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.430
No, you are suspicious.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.400
That's why I'm so happy!

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.830
Well, I guess it's OK.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:41.190
That's right! You haven't decided on a piece yet!

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:43.820
I'll grant you a bunch of musical scores!

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:47.510
That's to show how I feel!

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.700
Well, we'll meet again, Kahoko Hino!

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.150
I'm not happy.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.550
He didn't have to give me all these.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.420
Don't say a word of this to anyone!

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.040
Do you mean about you playing the... piano?

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:06.890
Why not?

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:18.560
I can't rescue you if you fall like last time.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.400
I'm fine.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.490
I'm counting you, I really am.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.010
Sorry about yesterday.

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.040
Huh?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:42.030
To make up for it, I can help you tune your instrument after school.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.100
Do you need my help?

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.890
Thank you!

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:55.030
He said he'd be better off if he quit,

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:57.690
but maybe just the opposite is true.

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:02.070
General Studies students?

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.620
What're they doing here?

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:06.790
Geez, all the Music students are staring at us...

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:09.470
Are you anti-Music students, Tsuchiura-kun?

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.450
I wouldn't say "anti."

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.420
But, they've never left a good taste in my mouth.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.210
How about whats-his-name...

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:18.940
Huh?

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:21.200
The one who brought you the handouts yesterday.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.960
Take care to not let the quality of your performance in the competition drop any, OK?

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.010
Oh, Tsukimori-kun? He's a second year.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.430
He's going to be playing the violin in the competition.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.650
Tsukimori, huh? He made them leave an even worse taste in my mouth.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:37.610
Well, I guess I understand how he can feel that way.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.080
Ah, it's this practice room.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.410
That was him, wasn't it?

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.160
The quality of her performance, huh?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.030
That's stupid.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.960
Are you saying people in General Studies don't?

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.220
He's got nothing to do with the competition,

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.500
so why is he so upset over it?

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.280
Though I suppose the same could be said about me.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.290
Wow, what a nice practice room.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:13.000
Anyway, think you can find a piece you want to play in that giant stack of scores there?

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.770
Huh? U-Umm...

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.690
I really have no idea which one might be good to play.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:23.320
I see. So it's not at a point where you'd need tuning yet.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.140
What's the theme?

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.100
"A Beginning".

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.980
A Beginning, huh?

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:31.990
That's pretty vague.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:37.920
That should leave you more room for interpretation, in any case.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.440
Oh, yeah. What were you playing again yesterday, "Fantasia"?

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:43.130
That was beautiful!

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:46.750
Is there a Chopin composition that can be played on the violin?

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:50.540
Chopin? Chopin and piano go hand in hand.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.550
They called him the poet of the piano.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:56.020
I see. What should I play?

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.220
It's not a matter of what you should play.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.020
Huh?

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:04.990
What matters is what and how you express a story through your song.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:08.450
What I express?

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:13.400
Well, for now, why don't I accompany you in the Gavotte you played the other day?

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.400
What? You heard me play?!

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.540
You did play it where everyone could see you.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.880
I'm so embarrassed!

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:25.430
You weren't bad.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.180
Minuet... Humoresque...

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.650
I really need to pick a song!

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:41.970
Hey, Mom! What are you doing outside of Kaho's room?

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:45.870
Oh, honey, she's been really odd lately.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:48.810
She's walking around with this huge bag.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.990
Do your best, Kahoko!

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.370
Hello.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:02.620
I'm here to return the umbrella I borrowed the other day.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.030
Oh, welcome.

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:08.730
I'm sorry. Are you busy or something?

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.750
Oh, these are just some things I scattered about.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:15.140
It's actually because Ryo played the piano the other day.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:19.110
Ryo? Oh, you mean Tsuchiura-kun, huh?

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:24.370
I remembered that I had a bunch of videos of him, so I've been looking for them.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:28.980
Ah, there we go. This is from when he was in grammar school.

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:28.980
Ryo - 11 Years Old

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.820
Care to watch it with me?

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.910
Come on, don't videotape me!

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:44.150
Now, I went and bought a video camera just for this. Just entertain me.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.630
Man, if I have to...

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.150
What?! That's Tsuchiura-kun?!

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:51.850
He's so tiny!

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:56.180
Yes, he was still small back then.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:59.270
I never expected he'd get so big.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:07.530
That's a grammar school student playing?

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:11.810
Yes, Ryo was incredibly gifted.

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:14.440
These are all recordings of Chopin.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.730
"Valse du Petit Chien" in black key.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:19.900
Come to think of it, the song he played the other day was Chopin, too.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.840
He continued to progress.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:24.310
We had high hopes for him to become a great pianist.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:26.980
He should play more often.

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:28.690
I agree!

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.220
Why is he on the soccer club?

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:33.810
Why is he hiding his skill when he's this talented?

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.060
It's such a waste!

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:42.510
But I'm sure it's not that simple.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.200
What is this I'm feeling?

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.140
I feel nostalgic,

00:09:58.140 --> 00:09:59.880
and yet sad...

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:03.830
I feel like the notes of the piano are softly carrying me away with them...

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.750
It makes me feel like I'm quietly rising up...

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:14.100
What? No... I'm sorry...

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:17.580
This piece was written by Chopin himself.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:22.680
He even said: "I have never written such a beautiful melody before."

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:28.240
They say he wrote this song out of love for his homeland, Poland.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:32.100
All right. How was that?

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:36.740
It really is a waste, Tsuchiura-kun.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:41.700
He did enter into a competition once as a kid,

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:44.410
but he ended up acting all irrationally.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:47.950
Since them, he won't play in public.

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:52.710
I don't think he hates the piano, though.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:56.840
I'd like to think there's something that caused him to be this way.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:01.550
Everyone can enjoy music.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:03.860
A Beginning...

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:06.130
Do you like Chopin?

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:08.830
Oh, I'm actually not that familiar with him.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:11.230
It's just that every song of his I've heard were great.

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:14.310
It's a shame I cannot play them on the violin.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:16.980
Huh? That's not true.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:20.990
I have scores of his songs that have been arranged for the violin.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:22.820
Seriously?!

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.580
Let's there...

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.580
There it is!

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:29.770
Here you go.

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:35.970
It's true that the piano is the first instrument that comes to mind when you talk about Chopin.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.050
It's really mysterious.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:43.890
When you turn these written notes into sounds, it becomes so beautiful.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:45.680
How can I put it?

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:50.860
It's like... the performer is resurrecting the music within.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:55.070
May I play this?

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:58.030
Of course! You're very welcome to do so!

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:03.040
Before I lose that sound from before...

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:22.560
I'd like to try playing some Chopin.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:25.380
Huh? Chopin?

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:29.050
Is it odd to play Chopin on the violin?

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:34.060
Oh, no. The best piece to play is the one you genuinely want to play.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.010
You think?

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:37.110
Yes!

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.530
All right, then!

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:43.410
For an amateur to start by playing Chopin...

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:48.360
Sure, she's in General Studies, but you can tell she's a participant in the competition.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.830
I wonder when she'll come here next.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:45.080
Tomorrow's the day, huh?

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:58.480
Hey, Shimizu.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:04.320
Kanamoto-sensei...

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.380
I told you, it's Kanazawa.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:08.520
Anyway, you doing good?

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:13.490
Yes. I eat my breakfast properly each morning.

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:16.490
No, that's not what I meant.

00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:18.070
Ah, never mind.

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:19.650
Anyway, do your best.

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:24.490
Yes, sir. Please do your best, too, Kanagawa-sensei.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:28.120
I told you, it's Kanazawa.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:31.700
And what do I have to "do my best" for?

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:39.180
Well, I hope things just stay nice and simple.

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:46.420
Ah, we've been practicing for two hours already.

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.310
Shall we call it a day?

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:50.360
What? That's it?

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:51.350
Hmm?

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:54.140
Never mind. Good work today.

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:57.340
Thank you. Sorry to keep you here so long.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.290
No, don't mention it!

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.900
It's really impressive that you've come so far along in such a short time.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:04.540
Do your best tomorrow.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:08.130
Way to put the pressure on.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:10.380
So tomorrow's it, huh?

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:14.520
What are you gonna wear? Gonna get all decked out?

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.380
That's the plan.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:19.530
Man, I hate that.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:20.970
I can't wear jeans?

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.320
I'm not sure about jeans...

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:26.340
What about the most expensive pair I own?

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:27.730
Most expensive pair, huh?

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.550
All right!

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:39.360
Tsuchiura, how about sharing the glory sometime?

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:42.180
All right! We'll definitely make it into the prefectural tournament this year!

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:44.070
We're counting on you, Tsuchiura!

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:50.110
Tomorrow's the day...

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.800
I don't have any confidence.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:57.460
Maybe I should practice a little more.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:02.050
There's a piano in there!

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:06.720
OK. I'll practice a little more in here.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:09.470
No one will come, I'm sure.

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:17.990
Ah, Tsuchiura-kun!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.460
Hino?

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:21.720
What are you doing in there?

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:24.370
See, the first performance is tomorrow,

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.790
so I figured I'd get a little more practice in.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:29.000
I see. Tomorrow, huh?

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:32.000
Oh, there's an upright in there.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.790
It's called an upright?

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:37.300
You're really clueless, huh?

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:40.010
Oh yeah! Why don't you play a song for me, Tsuchiura-kun?

00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:40.790
What?

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:44.340
No one will be listening. Just one song to cheer me up for tomorrow!

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:47.850
Stingy.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:48.970
Sheesh.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:51.150
If I have to.

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:03.240
It's in pretty good shape.

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:05.010
Well, any requests?

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:06.320
Huh?

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:09.240
Then... Chopin!

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:11.340
Chopin, huh?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.340
You got it!

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:28.240
Ah... This is the song he played in that video when he was a little boy.

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:34.230
The song from then and the song from now are overlapping...

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.440
That's "Valse du Petit Chien," isn't it?

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:40.560
It's so cute how the notes roll all around!

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.700
Yeah, true to its name.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:45.700
But it's really interesting...

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:48.570
To hear your performance from now and back then.

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:49.990
Back then?

00:17:49.990 --> 00:17:52.630
You know, when you were in grammar school.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:53.780
Where'd you hear that?

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:54.660
Minami Instruments.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:07.420
See, there was this video of you playing when I went there the other day.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:08.490
Video?!

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:10.600
I saw it.

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.320
Don't "I saw it" me!

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:15.230
That old bum...

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:18.550
It's fine! You were really cute.

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:20.600
Don't try and salvage the situation.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:22.290
Damn...

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:25.560
But that video was really shocking.

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:27.750
You were so gifted.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:30.810
If you had that much talent at such a young age,

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:33.770
I bet you could have been a professional pianist.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:36.720
It's not that simple.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:40.140
Yeah, I suppose in reality, that's true.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.750
But it never crossed your mind?

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:49.130
If you want to win the competitions, then you need to play classical music, right?

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:53.000
It's what all the Music Department kids strive for.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.440
Winning in the competition can really take you places.

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:57.410
That's their motivation, right?

00:18:57.410 --> 00:18:59.550
I don't care for that.

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:01.720
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:05.480
Don't the characters for "music" in your language, Japanese, mean "to enjoy sound"?

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:08.130
I think...

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:11.110
I think the competition may be a bit different this time.

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:14.960
It's not just about who wins.

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:17.210
That's how I feel.

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:21.570
Sorry, you're participating in it too, huh?

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.470
Let's stop talking about it.

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.380
That's not what I...

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:30.840
Why do you hide your talent? I don't understand.

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:34.490
I mean, you look like you want to play more.

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:40.970
I wonder if you might even be interested in the competition.

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:42.610
Not at all...

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:47.070
So I wondered if maybe that's why you're so worried about me.

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:49.470
Not at all!

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:55.170
How about you worry about yourself instead of others for a change?

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:57.550
The competition is tomorrow, isn't it?

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:18.070
Oh no... What got into me?

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:26.260
I'm in no position to talk about others...

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:35.080
I don't understand why I was chosen myself.

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.300
Violin?

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:25.860
What gentle music.

00:21:43.770 --> 00:21:46.610
OK, everyone. Get home safe now.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:48.050
See you!

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:48.960
Bye bye!

00:21:55.390 --> 00:21:57.580
Good luck tomorrow.

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:00.080
Huh?

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.700
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:39.670
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:44.900
Since the piano has a rather large range,

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:48.500
most all classic songs can be played on it.

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:51.280
Its proper name is "pianoforte,"

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:54.030
so it's been shortened to just "piano".

00:23:54.590 --> 00:23:56.560
The wide one is a grand piano.

00:23:56.560 --> 00:23:59.890
The vertical upright piano is the second type.

00:23:59.890 --> 00:24:01.630
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:24:01.630 --> 00:24:05.110
How many keys does a piano have?

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:09.750
Next Episode

00:24:05.910 --> 00:24:08.630
Huh? Why is everyone all dressed up?

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:09.750
No one told me about this!

00:24:09.750 --> 00:24:12.430
What're you doing?! Hurry and get changed!

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:15.090
But I don't like these clothes!

00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:18.220
Next episode: Barefoot Vibrato.

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:20.050
Ouch, I'm getting a blister.

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:22.010
The answer is...

00:24:22.620 --> 00:24:25.070
88 keys!
